---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: "File storage, uploads and share links | Shellui"
description: "Add file uploads, browsing, and sharing to your Shellui apps. Connect storage-service for file permissions, share links, and storage limits."
eyebrow: Features
heading: "File storage your apps can share"
lede: "Connect storage-service to upload, browse, and share files across your apps. Use the software development kit (SDK) for file operations and the Files app for browsing and selection. Manage access and storage limits at the company level."
---

<div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Connect your apps to a shared file store</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2" href="{{ site.storageService }}">storage-service</a> backend stores files in Amazon S3-compatible storage or on your server's filesystem. It verifies the signed-in account and enforces company and optional per-user storage limits.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Your apps call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.storage</code> through the SDK. The shell sends each request to the configured storage service with the signed-in account's access token.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-xs">
    {% include "feature-visual-storage.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-10 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink">1. Connect storage</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">storage.url</code> to your storage service. Add <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">filesUrl</code> to connect the Files explorer and picker.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink">2. Check storage usage</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">See current usage in Settings → Storage. You can hide this settings page while keeping storage available in Administration and through the SDK.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink">3. Work with files</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">After <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">init</code>, upload, list, move, and download through <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">shellui.storage.from("company")</code>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
  {% highlight "json", "shellui.config.json" %}
{
  "storage": {
    "url": "http://localhost:8001",
    "filesUrl": "http://localhost:5175/"
  }
}
    {% endhighlight %}
</div>

{# Future screenshot: Playground Files explorer. Add a real image here when available. #}

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="files-from-iframe">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="files-from-iframe" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Upload and select files from your app</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Use the SDK to upload, list, move, and download files. Calls return <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">{ data, error }</code> so your app can handle failures. The file picker opens the Files app in a shell modal for selecting files or folders.</p>
  </div>
  <article tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="upload-card-title" class="anim-card mt-10 flex min-w-0 flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-card focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary md:flex-row">
    <div class="p-6 md:flex md:w-2/5 md:flex-col md:justify-center">
      <h3 id="upload-card-title" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">Upload progress in the shell</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Uploads appear in a shell toast with progress for each file. People keep working while files finish, can cancel one, and see which file failed.</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Hover or focus the card to play it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="anim-visual relative border-t border-border bg-muted md:w-3/5 md:border-t-0 md:border-l" data-anim-play>
      {% include "feature-visual-upload.njk" %}
      <button type="button" class="anim-play" aria-label="Play upload animation">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="anim-ring" cx="20" cy="20" r="19"/><circle class="anim-ring-fill" cx="20" cy="20" r="19" pathLength="100"/><path class="anim-icon" d="M16 13.5v13l10.5-6.5z"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  </article>
  {% include "storage-sdk-examples.njk" %}
</section>
<script src="/assets/js/anim-card.js" type="module"></script>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="private-by-default">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="private-by-default" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Control who can access each file</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Each company has a file collection, or bucket, named <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">company</code>. New items at the root are private to their creator; items inside folders inherit the folder's permissions. Share selected files and folders with members, or create a share link for someone outside the company.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-6 lg:gap-8">
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Access grants</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Grant or deny read, write, or administration access to a file or folder. Apply permissions to individual accounts or the whole company.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Share links</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Share an individual file with a link that needs no account. Set an expiry, a download limit, or both, and revoke the link when access is no longer needed.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Quotas</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Set a total storage limit for the company and optional limits per account. The service rejects uploads that exceed those limits, and Settings shows current usage.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="storage-events">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="storage-events" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Events, webhooks, and email</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">When you set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">EMAIL_SERVICE_API_KEY</code>, storage posts events to email-service and stores every event for the event log. Webhook and email bodies omit tokens, sign-in links, signed URLs, and other secrets. Company owners manage the rules in <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2" href="/features/administration/#webhooks">Administration</a>.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The storage image runs webhook retries every minute and an hourly data purge. It does not need cron. In production, set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">REDIS_URL</code> or the container does not start. Scheduler metrics stay on the staff metrics endpoint.</p>
  </div>
</section>

